From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 03 Nov 2026 17:00:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: sc8547_svooc: separate the session from the
 VOOC exchange

The session driver interleaves two things. One is the session: the
charge-level gate, the buck handoff, the 50 ms sampling, the running
checks, the teardown order and the restore of the input. The other is
the SuperVOOC exchange: the D+/D- mux, the PHY, the handshake, the
frames and their timeouts, and the way a new current is asked for (as
the reply to the next battery query). A PD PPS back-end for the same
pumps shares the first and replaces the second (the PD PPS plan,
revision 2, section 4.1, one driver with two adapter back-ends), and
three numbers that read as protocol-neutral belong to the adapter: the
buck must be seen idle with VBUS at 4.5 to 5.5 V because a VOOC adapter
holds 5 V until it is granted; the input is given back once VBUS is
down to 5.5 V because the adapter drops back to 5 V when the replies
stop; and VBUS above 5.5 V before the grant is a protocol error. A PPS
session starts from the 9 V contract and lifts VBUS itself before the
first enable (section 4.3), so each of the three differs there, while
the other half of the pre-grant rule, that no pump switches before it
is enabled, holds for every protocol (review item S-10).

Introduce struct svooc_adapter_ops and make the VOOC exchange its first
instance. The session calls setup (take the link: the mux and the PHY,
with the pumps prepared), start (begin the exchange under the lock with
the session initialised: the protocol reset and the handshake write),
tick (the protocol's own timeouts: the adapter's frames, the current
acknowledgment, the change), busy (a change is still in flight: the
one-at-a-time gate, consulted before the ramp arithmetic where the gate
was), change (ask for a current; it returns an errno because the PD PPS
request is a firmware write that can fail, 0 here), stop (the PHY off,
svooc_phy_stop() itself: after the pumps once a session ran, before
them when setup failed) and restore (the mux released). start is split
from setup because the link can fail before a session exists: that
failure is undone without the wakeup source and recorded as a failed
session, the error kept and the state set to DONE under the lock,
exactly as before; the handshake, on the other hand, must be written
after the session is initialised, under the lock. Section 4.3 of the
plan named five operations and now carries a status note recording
these seven. The session's own clearing of phy_on, proto.permit and
pending_ua stays in svooc_stop_locked(), under the lock, where it was.
The quiet window, the restore condition and the pre-grant ceiling are
fields of the back-end, and the two checks that use them join the
policy library's header as inlines next to vbat_uv(), with the 25 mA
named. The PD PPS numbers to come are named in the same header rather
than in the test: the 9.5 V the session plans to ask for at most, the
10.0 V rail it never asks for, the 200 mV a request may be exceeded by
before the grant, and the 4.5 to 9.5 V window in which its buck must
be seen idle, with the pre-grant ceiling, the request plus the margin
and never above the rail, as an inline the PPS back-end will call.
Nothing in the driver uses them yet. KUnit cases pin the VOOC numbers
and the PPS ones. The back-end is chosen from the charger type when a
session starts: a dedicated or Apple-brick charger inside the VOOC
back-end's own 4.5 to 5.5 V is a SuperVOOC adapter, anything else no
session, as before.

No behaviour changes. Every I2C write, mux operation, supply read and
property write happens in the same order with the same operands, every
message prints the same text ("SuperVOOC" comes from the back-end's
name), and the supply, debugfs and sysfs are untouched. The regulation
keeps the instruction order of the original, gate before ramp
arithmetic before the three writes. Two things moved within orders that
nothing observes: the VOOC counters are reset after the session's own
fields instead of among them, inside the same lock section, which the
PHY interrupt cannot enter before the unlock; and the protocol's three
-ETIMEDOUT checks run before the 30 s pre-running timeout instead of
around it, all four returning the same errno. The KUnit suite grows to
15 cases, all passing on the host.

Signed-off-by: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy.h      |   65 +++++
 drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy_test.c |   62 +++++
 drivers/power/supply/sc8547_svooc.c              |  262 ++++++++++++++++------
 3 files changed, 316 insertions(+), 73 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy.h b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy.h
index d517d1a..808f1fd 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy.h
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy.h
@@ -21,6 +21,18 @@
 #define SC8547_DIRECT_POWER_SETTLE_UW	54500000LL
 /* A session ends normally at this charge level, in percent. */
 #define SC8547_DIRECT_CAPACITY_END	90
+/* The buck has let go of the input when it draws no more than this. */
+#define SC8547_DIRECT_QUIET_UA		25000
+/*
+ * The PD PPS session to come: the most it plans to ask for, the input rail,
+ * which is never an operating point, how far above a request VBUS may run
+ * before the grant, and the window in which its buck may be seen idle.
+ */
+#define SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_CAP_UV		9500000
+#define SC8547_DIRECT_RAIL_UV			10000000
+#define SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_PREGRANT_MARGIN_UV	200000
+#define SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MIN_UV		4500000
+#define SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MAX_UV		9500000
 
 enum sc8547_direct_therm {
 	SC8547_DIRECT_USB_CONNECTOR,
@@ -87,4 +99,57 @@ static inline int sc8547_direct_vbat_uv(int gauge_uv, int pump_uv)
 	return max(gauge_uv, pump_uv);
 }
 
+/**
+ * sc8547_direct_quiet() - the buck has let go of the input
+ * @usb_ua: the current the USB supply reports drawing
+ * @usb_uv: its voltage
+ * @min_uv: the lowest voltage the adapter holds before the pumps take over
+ * @max_uv: the highest
+ *
+ * The pumps may only take an input that the buck has stopped drawing from,
+ * at the voltage the adapter's protocol leaves it at before the grant.
+ *
+ * Return: true when the buck draws at most 25 mA at a voltage inside
+ * [@min_uv, @max_uv].
+ */
+static inline bool sc8547_direct_quiet(int usb_ua, int usb_uv, int min_uv,
+				       int max_uv)
+{
+	return usb_ua <= SC8547_DIRECT_QUIET_UA && usb_uv >= min_uv &&
+	       usb_uv <= max_uv;
+}
+
+/**
+ * sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok() - the pumps before the adapter is granted
+ * @switching: the main pump is switching
+ * @vbus_uv: its input voltage
+ * @max_uv: the highest voltage the adapter's protocol allows before the grant
+ *
+ * A pump must not switch before it is enabled, whatever the protocol; how
+ * high the adapter may hold VBUS depends on it.
+ *
+ * Return: 0, or -EPROTO.
+ */
+static inline int sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(bool switching, int vbus_uv,
+					    int max_uv)
+{
+	return switching || vbus_uv > max_uv ? -EPROTO : 0;
+}
+
+/**
+ * sc8547_direct_pps_pregrant_max_uv() - the PD PPS ceiling before the grant
+ * @request_uv: the voltage last requested from the source
+ *
+ * A PPS source may run a margin above what it was asked for; the rail itself
+ * is never an operating point.
+ *
+ * Return: the highest VBUS allowed before the grant, for
+ * sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok().
+ */
+static inline int sc8547_direct_pps_pregrant_max_uv(int request_uv)
+{
+	return min(request_uv + SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_PREGRANT_MARGIN_UV,
+		   SC8547_DIRECT_RAIL_UV);
+}
+
 #endif
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy_test.c b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy_test.c
index 92dc0a2..f92f26f 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy_test.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_direct_policy_test.c
@@ -36,6 +36,12 @@ static void sc8547_direct_test_constants(struct kunit *test)
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, SC8547_DIRECT_DIE_MAX_DC, 700);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, SC8547_DIRECT_POWER_SETTLE_UW, 54500000LL);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, SC8547_DIRECT_CAPACITY_END, 90);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, SC8547_DIRECT_QUIET_UA, 25000);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_CAP_UV, 9500000);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, SC8547_DIRECT_RAIL_UV, 10000000);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_PREGRANT_MARGIN_UV, 200000);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MIN_UV, 4500000);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MAX_UV, 9500000);
 
 	/*
 	 * Soft to hard: usb connector 60-70, battery connector 60-70,
@@ -564,6 +570,60 @@ static void sc8547_direct_test_second(struct kunit *test)
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, sc8547_direct_second_shared(&m, &s));
 }
 
+/* The buck is quiet at 25 mA or less, with VBUS in the adapter's window. */
+static void sc8547_direct_test_quiet(struct kunit *test)
+{
+	/* A SuperVOOC adapter holds 5 V before the grant: 4.5 to 5.5 V. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(25000, 5000000, 4500000, 5500000));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(0, 4500000, 4500000, 5500000));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(-100000, 5500000, 4500000, 5500000));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(25001, 5000000, 4500000, 5500000));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(0, 4499999, 4500000, 5500000));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(0, 5500001, 4500000, 5500000));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(0, 9000000, 4500000, 5500000));
+	/* A PD PPS session starts from the 9 V contract: 4.5 to 9.5 V. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(0, 9000000, SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MIN_UV,
+						    SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MAX_UV));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(25000, 9500000, SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MIN_UV,
+						    SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MAX_UV));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(0, 4500000, SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MIN_UV,
+						    SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MAX_UV));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(0, 9500001, SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MIN_UV,
+						     SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MAX_UV));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(0, 4499999, SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MIN_UV,
+						     SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MAX_UV));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, sc8547_direct_quiet(25001, 9000000, SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MIN_UV,
+						     SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_QUIET_MAX_UV));
+}
+
+/* No pump switches before the grant, and VBUS stays under the protocol's ceiling. */
+static void sc8547_direct_test_pregrant(struct kunit *test)
+{
+	int max;
+
+	/* SuperVOOC: the adapter holds 5 V, 5.5 V at most. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(false, 5000000, 5500000), 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(false, 5500000, 5500000), 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(false, 5500001, 5500000), -EPROTO);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(false, 8000000, 5500000), -EPROTO);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(true, 5000000, 5500000), -EPROTO);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(true, 0, 5500000), -EPROTO);
+
+	/* PD PPS: the request plus 200 mV, never above the 10.0 V rail. */
+	max = sc8547_direct_pps_pregrant_max_uv(8200000);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, max, 8400000);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(false, 8300000, max), 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(false, 8400000, max), 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(false, 8400001, max), -EPROTO);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(true, 8300000, max), -EPROTO);
+	/* The planned maximum keeps its margin; a request near the rail does not. */
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pps_pregrant_max_uv(SC8547_DIRECT_PPS_CAP_UV), 9700000);
+	max = sc8547_direct_pps_pregrant_max_uv(9900000);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, max, SC8547_DIRECT_RAIL_UV);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(false, 10000000, max), 0);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, sc8547_direct_pregrant_ok(false, 10000001, max), -EPROTO);
+}
+
 static struct kunit_case sc8547_direct_test_cases[] = {
 	KUNIT_CASE(sc8547_direct_test_constants),
 	KUNIT_CASE(sc8547_direct_test_scale),
@@ -578,6 +638,8 @@ static struct kunit_case sc8547_direct_test_cases[] = {
 	KUNIT_CASE(sc8547_direct_test_running_current),
 	KUNIT_CASE(sc8547_direct_test_running_disagree),
 	KUNIT_CASE(sc8547_direct_test_second),
+	KUNIT_CASE(sc8547_direct_test_quiet),
+	KUNIT_CASE(sc8547_direct_test_pregrant),
 	{}
 };
 
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_svooc.c b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_svooc.c
index 2d57991..9871f82 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_svooc.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc8547_svooc.c
@@ -97,6 +97,42 @@ static const char * const svooc_state_names[] = {
 	"stopping", "done",
 };
 
+struct sc8547_svooc;
+
+/**
+ * struct svooc_adapter_ops - an adapter protocol behind the shared session
+ * @name: the protocol, for messages.
+ * @quiet_min_uv: the lowest VBUS at which the buck may be seen idle before the
+ *	pumps take over.
+ * @quiet_max_uv: the highest such VBUS.
+ * @restore_max_uv: the input is given back once VBUS is down to this.
+ * @pregrant_max_uv: VBUS may not exceed this before the adapter is granted.
+ * @setup: take the adapter's link, with the pumps prepared; a failure is
+ *	undone by @stop and @restore.
+ * @start: begin the exchange, under the lock, with the session initialised.
+ * @tick: the protocol's own checks on every tick, at @now.
+ * @busy: a current change is still in flight; none is asked for meanwhile.
+ * @change: ask the adapter for a current; a negative return stops the
+ *	session.
+ * @stop: the link off; after the pumps once a session ran, before them when
+ *	@setup failed.
+ * @restore: give the link back.
+ */
+struct svooc_adapter_ops {
+	const char *name;
+	int quiet_min_uv;
+	int quiet_max_uv;
+	int restore_max_uv;
+	int pregrant_max_uv;
+	int (*setup)(struct sc8547_svooc *sv);
+	int (*start)(struct sc8547_svooc *sv);
+	int (*tick)(struct sc8547_svooc *sv, unsigned long now);
+	bool (*busy)(struct sc8547_svooc *sv);
+	int (*change)(struct sc8547_svooc *sv, int ua);
+	int (*stop)(struct sc8547_svooc *sv);
+	int (*restore)(struct sc8547_svooc *sv);
+};
+
 struct sc8547_svooc {
 	struct device *dev;
 	struct sc8547 *main;
@@ -112,6 +148,8 @@ struct sc8547_svooc {
 	struct dentry *debugfs;
 	/* Serializes the session between the PHY interrupt and the worker. */
 	struct mutex lock;
+	/* The adapter protocol of the session, chosen when it starts. */
+	const struct svooc_adapter_ops *ops;
 	struct oplus_svooc proto;
 	enum svooc_state state;
 	enum power_supply_charge_type mode;
@@ -207,19 +245,6 @@ static int svooc_read_therms(struct sc8547_svooc *sv, int *mc)
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static bool svooc_charger(struct sc8547_svooc *sv, int *vbus_uv)
-{
-	int online, type;
-
-	if (svooc_get(sv->usb, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ONLINE, &online) || !online ||
-	    svooc_get(sv->usb, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_USB_TYPE, &type) ||
-	    svooc_get(sv->usb, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW, vbus_uv))
-		return false;
-	/* SuperVOOC adapters present as a dedicated or proprietary charger. */
-	return type == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_DCP ||
-	       type == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_APPLE_BRICK_ID;
-}
-
 /* The hotter die of the pumps in use. */
 static int svooc_die(struct sc8547_svooc *sv)
 {
@@ -308,16 +333,17 @@ static void svooc_stop_locked(struct sc8547_svooc *sv, int error)
 		return;
 	sv->error = error;
 	if (error)
-		dev_warn(sv->dev, "SuperVOOC stopped in %s: %d (rx %02x flags %02x)\n",
-			 svooc_state_names[sv->state], error, sv->rx, sv->flags);
+		dev_warn(sv->dev, "%s stopped in %s: %d (rx %02x flags %02x)\n",
+			 sv->ops->name, svooc_state_names[sv->state], error, sv->rx,
+			 sv->flags);
 	else
-		dev_info(sv->dev, "SuperVOOC finished\n");
+		dev_info(sv->dev, "%s finished\n", sv->ops->name);
 	if (sv->second && sc8547_disable(sv->second))
 		dev_crit(sv->dev, "cannot stop the second pump\n");
 	if (sc8547_disable(sv->main))
 		dev_crit(sv->dev, "cannot stop the main pump\n");
 	sv->phy_on = false;
-	if (svooc_phy_stop(sv))
+	if (sv->ops->stop(sv))
 		dev_err(sv->dev, "cannot stop the VOOC PHY\n");
 	sv->proto.permit = false;
 	sv->second_on = false;
@@ -517,13 +543,125 @@ static void svooc_phy_irq(void *data)
 	mutex_unlock(&sv->lock);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The SuperVOOC exchange: the adapter asks over D+/D- through the pump's
+ * PHY and is answered from the PHY interrupt above. What follows is the
+ * back-end the shared session calls.
+ */
+static int svooc_vooc_setup(struct sc8547_svooc *sv)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = mux_state_try_select(sv->dpdm);
+	sv->route = !ret;
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = svooc_phy_setup(sv);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static int svooc_vooc_start(struct sc8547_svooc *sv)
+{
+	oplus_svooc_reset(&sv->proto);
+	sv->frames = 0;
+	sv->irqs = 0;
+	sv->ignored = 0;
+	sv->worst_us = 0;
+	sv->rx = 0;
+	sv->flags = 0;
+	sv->skipped = 0;
+	sv->last_rx = jiffies;
+	sv->phy_on = true;
+	/* The handshake starts the adapter talking: be ready first. */
+	return regmap_write(sv->regmap, SC8547_VOOC_CTRL, 0x81);
+}
+
+/* The adapter keeps asking, and acknowledges each current in time. */
+static int svooc_vooc_tick(struct sc8547_svooc *sv, unsigned long now)
+{
+	int frame_ms = sv->frames ? SVOOC_FRAME_MS : SVOOC_FIRST_FRAME_MS;
+
+	if (time_after(now, sv->last_rx + msecs_to_jiffies(frame_ms)))
+		return -ETIMEDOUT;
+	if (sv->pending_ua && time_after(now, sv->ack_deadline))
+		return -ETIMEDOUT;
+	if (sv->change && time_after(now, sv->change_deadline))
+		return -ETIMEDOUT;
+	return 0;
+}
+
+/* One change at a time, at most one a second. */
+static bool svooc_vooc_busy(struct sc8547_svooc *sv)
+{
+	return sv->pending_ua || sv->change ||
+	       time_before(jiffies, sv->change_deadline);
+}
+
+/*
+ * A change goes out as the reply to the next battery query, which makes the
+ * adapter ask for the current.
+ */
+static int svooc_vooc_change(struct sc8547_svooc *sv, int ua)
+{
+	sv->target_ua = ua;
+	sv->change = true;
+	sv->change_deadline = jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(SVOOC_CHANGE_MS);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int svooc_vooc_restore(struct sc8547_svooc *sv)
+{
+	int ret = 0;
+
+	if (sv->route) {
+		ret = mux_state_deselect(sv->dpdm);
+		sv->route = false;
+	}
+	return ret;
+}
+
+/* The adapter holds 5 V until it is granted and drops back to it after. */
+static const struct svooc_adapter_ops svooc_vooc_ops = {
+	.name = "SuperVOOC",
+	.quiet_min_uv = 4500000,
+	.quiet_max_uv = 5500000,
+	.restore_max_uv = 5500000,
+	.pregrant_max_uv = 5500000,
+	.setup = svooc_vooc_setup,
+	.start = svooc_vooc_start,
+	.tick = svooc_vooc_tick,
+	.busy = svooc_vooc_busy,
+	.change = svooc_vooc_change,
+	.stop = svooc_phy_stop,
+	.restore = svooc_vooc_restore,
+};
+
+/* The adapter protocol the charger calls for, or NULL. */
+static const struct svooc_adapter_ops *svooc_adapter(struct sc8547_svooc *sv)
+{
+	int online, type, vbus;
+
+	if (svooc_get(sv->usb, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ONLINE, &online) || !online ||
+	    svooc_get(sv->usb, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_USB_TYPE, &type) ||
+	    svooc_get(sv->usb, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW, &vbus))
+		return NULL;
+	/* SuperVOOC adapters present as a dedicated or proprietary charger at 5 V. */
+	if ((type == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_DCP ||
+	     type == POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_APPLE_BRICK_ID) &&
+	    vbus >= svooc_vooc_ops.quiet_min_uv && vbus <= svooc_vooc_ops.quiet_max_uv)
+		return &svooc_vooc_ops;
+	return NULL;
+}
+
 static void svooc_start(struct sc8547_svooc *sv)
 {
+	const struct svooc_adapter_ops *ops;
 	struct sc8547_direct_battery bat;
-	int therm[SC8547_DIRECT_THERMS], vbus, ret;
+	int therm[SC8547_DIRECT_THERMS], ret;
 
-	if (sv->mode != POWER_SUPPLY_CHARGE_TYPE_FAST || !svooc_charger(sv, &vbus) ||
-	    vbus < 4500000 || vbus > 5500000)
+	if (sv->mode != POWER_SUPPLY_CHARGE_TYPE_FAST)
+		return;
+	ops = svooc_adapter(sv);
+	if (!ops)
 		return;
 	if (time_before(jiffies, sv->plugged_at + msecs_to_jiffies(SVOOC_PLUG_MS))) {
 		mod_delayed_work(system_highpri_wq, &sv->work,
@@ -534,6 +672,7 @@ static void svooc_start(struct sc8547_svooc *sv)
 		return;
 
 	mutex_lock(&sv->lock);
+	sv->ops = ops;
 	sv->bat = bat;
 	memcpy(sv->therm_mc, therm, sizeof(therm));
 	memset(sv->sample, 0, sizeof(sv->sample));
@@ -551,21 +690,15 @@ static void svooc_start(struct sc8547_svooc *sv)
